# v2 (docs/specs/mastering-tools.md §5.3, M3): per band its channel, a shape, and dynamics, at the end so old songs
# and presets keep their sound (the defaults are v1's: Stereo, Standard, Off); then Delta.
group Channel and dynamics 1
B1Chan    "B1 channel"   0 4    0   enum Stereo Left Right Mid Side | Band 1: which channel it works on. Stereo: both (as v1); Left or Right: that one alone; Mid or Side: the mid (L+R)/2 or the side (L−R)/2 alone, the other untouched (mid/side encoded and decoded around the band)
B1Shape   "B1 shape"     0 4    0   enum Standard Proportional_Q Baxandall Vintage All-pass | Band 1: Standard: the type as it is (as v1). Proportional Q: a bell narrows as its gain grows (Q × 10^(|gain|/40): about twice as narrow for every 12 dB). Baxandall: a shelf becomes first order, 6 dB/oct, the gentle tone-control curve (Q unused). Vintage: a shelf gets its complementary dip, Pultec-style: a bell of half its gain the other way, Q 1, an octave above a low shelf or below a high shelf. All-pass: whatever the type, the band only turns the phase (second order at its frequency, Q its width)
B1Dyn     "B1 dynamic"   0 2    0   enum Off Down Up | Band 1 dynamic EQ (bells and shelves): Down: above the threshold the band's gain moves down (compresses what it hears), Up: it moves up; by the ratio, at most Range. The detector hears the band's own shape (a band-pass for a bell, low-pass for a low shelf, high-pass for a high shelf). Off: static (as v1)
B1Thresh  "B1 threshold" 0 600  300 lin -60 0 dB 1 | Band 1 dynamic: the level the band's detector must pass before its gain moves (dBFS, the envelope of what it hears)
B1Ratio   "B1 ratio"     0 1000 463 ratio 1 20 inf | Band 1 dynamic: the gain moves by 1 − 1/ratio dB for each dB over the threshold (∞: all of it)
B1Knee    "B1 knee"      0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 1 dynamic: width of the soft knee around the threshold
B1Range   "B1 range"     0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 1 dynamic: the most the gain moves from its setting
B1Attack  "B1 attack"    0 1000 639 time 0.00005 0.2 | Band 1 dynamic: time to 63 % of a gain change
B1Release "B1 release"   0 1000 532 time 0.005 3 | Band 1 dynamic: time back to 37 % of a gain change
B1Detect  "B1 detector"  0 1    0   enum Band Sidechain | Band 1 dynamic: Band: the detector hears the band's own input; Sidechain: the machine's second input (connect a machine to it), through the same shape and channel
group Channel and dynamics 2
B2Chan    "B2 channel"   0 4    0   enum Stereo Left Right Mid Side | Band 2: which channel it works on. Stereo: both (as v1); Left or Right: that one alone; Mid or Side: the mid (L+R)/2 or the side (L−R)/2 alone, the other untouched (mid/side encoded and decoded around the band)
B2Shape   "B2 shape"     0 4    0   enum Standard Proportional_Q Baxandall Vintage All-pass | Band 2: Standard: the type as it is (as v1). Proportional Q: a bell narrows as its gain grows (Q × 10^(|gain|/40): about twice as narrow for every 12 dB). Baxandall: a shelf becomes first order, 6 dB/oct, the gentle tone-control curve (Q unused). Vintage: a shelf gets its complementary dip, Pultec-style: a bell of half its gain the other way, Q 1, an octave above a low shelf or below a high shelf. All-pass: whatever the type, the band only turns the phase (second order at its frequency, Q its width)
B2Dyn     "B2 dynamic"   0 2    0   enum Off Down Up | Band 2 dynamic EQ (bells and shelves): Down: above the threshold the band's gain moves down (compresses what it hears), Up: it moves up; by the ratio, at most Range. The detector hears the band's own shape (a band-pass for a bell, low-pass for a low shelf, high-pass for a high shelf). Off: static (as v1)
B2Thresh  "B2 threshold" 0 600  300 lin -60 0 dB 1 | Band 2 dynamic: the level the band's detector must pass before its gain moves (dBFS, the envelope of what it hears)
B2Ratio   "B2 ratio"     0 1000 463 ratio 1 20 inf | Band 2 dynamic: the gain moves by 1 − 1/ratio dB for each dB over the threshold (∞: all of it)
B2Knee    "B2 knee"      0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 2 dynamic: width of the soft knee around the threshold
B2Range   "B2 range"     0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 2 dynamic: the most the gain moves from its setting
B2Attack  "B2 attack"    0 1000 639 time 0.00005 0.2 | Band 2 dynamic: time to 63 % of a gain change
B2Release "B2 release"   0 1000 532 time 0.005 3 | Band 2 dynamic: time back to 37 % of a gain change
B2Detect  "B2 detector"  0 1    0   enum Band Sidechain | Band 2 dynamic: Band: the detector hears the band's own input; Sidechain: the machine's second input (connect a machine to it), through the same shape and channel
