B6Ratio   "B6 ratio"     0 1000 463 ratio 1 20 inf | Band 6 dynamic: the gain moves by 1 − 1/ratio dB for each dB over the threshold (∞: all of it)
B6Knee    "B6 knee"      0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 6 dynamic: width of the soft knee around the threshold
B6Range   "B6 range"     0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 6 dynamic: the most the gain moves from its setting
B6Attack  "B6 attack"    0 1000 639 time 0.00005 0.2 | Band 6 dynamic: time to 63 % of a gain change
B6Release "B6 release"   0 1000 532 time 0.005 3 | Band 6 dynamic: time back to 37 % of a gain change
B6Detect  "B6 detector"  0 1    0   enum Band Sidechain | Band 6 dynamic: Band: the detector hears the band's own input; Sidechain: the machine's second input (connect a machine to it), through the same shape and channel
group Channel and dynamics 7
B7Chan    "B7 channel"   0 4    0   enum Stereo Left Right Mid Side | Band 7: which channel it works on. Stereo: both (as v1); Left or Right: that one alone; Mid or Side: the mid (L+R)/2 or the side (L−R)/2 alone, the other untouched (mid/side encoded and decoded around the band)
B7Shape   "B7 shape"     0 4    0   enum Standard Proportional_Q Baxandall Vintage All-pass | Band 7: Standard: the type as it is (as v1). Proportional Q: a bell narrows as its gain grows (Q × 10^(|gain|/40): about twice as narrow for every 12 dB). Baxandall: a shelf becomes first order, 6 dB/oct, the gentle tone-control curve (Q unused). Vintage: a shelf gets its complementary dip, Pultec-style: a bell of half its gain the other way, Q 1, an octave above a low shelf or below a high shelf. All-pass: whatever the type, the band only turns the phase (second order at its frequency, Q its width)
B7Dyn     "B7 dynamic"   0 2    0   enum Off Down Up | Band 7 dynamic EQ (bells and shelves): Down: above the threshold the band's gain moves down (compresses what it hears), Up: it moves up; by the ratio, at most Range. The detector hears the band's own shape (a band-pass for a bell, low-pass for a low shelf, high-pass for a high shelf). Off: static (as v1)
B7Thresh  "B7 threshold" 0 600  300 lin -60 0 dB 1 | Band 7 dynamic: the level the band's detector must pass before its gain moves (dBFS, the envelope of what it hears)
B7Ratio   "B7 ratio"     0 1000 463 ratio 1 20 inf | Band 7 dynamic: the gain moves by 1 − 1/ratio dB for each dB over the threshold (∞: all of it)
B7Knee    "B7 knee"      0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 7 dynamic: width of the soft knee around the threshold
B7Range   "B7 range"     0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 7 dynamic: the most the gain moves from its setting
B7Attack  "B7 attack"    0 1000 639 time 0.00005 0.2 | Band 7 dynamic: time to 63 % of a gain change
B7Release "B7 release"   0 1000 532 time 0.005 3 | Band 7 dynamic: time back to 37 % of a gain change
B7Detect  "B7 detector"  0 1    0   enum Band Sidechain | Band 7 dynamic: Band: the detector hears the band's own input; Sidechain: the machine's second input (connect a machine to it), through the same shape and channel
group Channel and dynamics 8
B8Chan    "B8 channel"   0 4    0   enum Stereo Left Right Mid Side | Band 8: which channel it works on. Stereo: both (as v1); Left or Right: that one alone; Mid or Side: the mid (L+R)/2 or the side (L−R)/2 alone, the other untouched (mid/side encoded and decoded around the band)
B8Shape   "B8 shape"     0 4    0   enum Standard Proportional_Q Baxandall Vintage All-pass | Band 8: Standard: the type as it is (as v1). Proportional Q: a bell narrows as its gain grows (Q × 10^(|gain|/40): about twice as narrow for every 12 dB). Baxandall: a shelf becomes first order, 6 dB/oct, the gentle tone-control curve (Q unused). Vintage: a shelf gets its complementary dip, Pultec-style: a bell of half its gain the other way, Q 1, an octave above a low shelf or below a high shelf. All-pass: whatever the type, the band only turns the phase (second order at its frequency, Q its width)
B8Dyn     "B8 dynamic"   0 2    0   enum Off Down Up | Band 8 dynamic EQ (bells and shelves): Down: above the threshold the band's gain moves down (compresses what it hears), Up: it moves up; by the ratio, at most Range. The detector hears the band's own shape (a band-pass for a bell, low-pass for a low shelf, high-pass for a high shelf). Off: static (as v1)
B8Thresh  "B8 threshold" 0 600  300 lin -60 0 dB 1 | Band 8 dynamic: the level the band's detector must pass before its gain moves (dBFS, the envelope of what it hears)
B8Ratio   "B8 ratio"     0 1000 463 ratio 1 20 inf | Band 8 dynamic: the gain moves by 1 − 1/ratio dB for each dB over the threshold (∞: all of it)
B8Knee    "B8 knee"      0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 8 dynamic: width of the soft knee around the threshold
B8Range   "B8 range"     0 240  60  lin 0 24 dB 1 | Band 8 dynamic: the most the gain moves from its setting
B8Attack  "B8 attack"    0 1000 639 time 0.00005 0.2 | Band 8 dynamic: time to 63 % of a gain change
B8Release "B8 release"   0 1000 532 time 0.005 3 | Band 8 dynamic: time back to 37 % of a gain change
B8Detect  "B8 detector"  0 1    0   enum Band Sidechain | Band 8 dynamic: Band: the detector hears the band's own input; Sidechain: the machine's second input (connect a machine to it), through the same shape and channel
group Monitor
Delta    "Delta"   0 1   0   switch | Hear only what the EQ changes: the output minus the input, before Output (zero latency, nothing to delay), gliding over 10 ms. Off for rendering

group Linear phase
Phase    "Phase"   0 1   0   enum Minimum Linear | Minimum: the bands as always, zero latency. Linear: one FIR from the bands' zero-phase magnitude (same dB at every frequency from 30 Hz, no phase turning, constant delay of 4095 + 512 samples at 44.1/48 kHz, reported to the host); Parametric mode only; dynamic bands are static in it; the Curve layer applies; a very narrow band at a low frequency is limited in Q (the editor says so)
Curve1  "Curve 1" 0 480 240 db -24 24 | Curve layer point 1 of 32 (log-spaced 20 Hz to 20 kHz, joined by a smooth curve), in dB, added to the bands before the linear-phase design (a match curve; Linear phase only)
Curve2  "Curve 2" 0 480 240 db -24 24 | Curve layer point 2 of 32 (log-spaced 20 Hz to 20 kHz, joined by a smooth curve), in dB, added to the bands before the linear-phase design (a match curve; Linear phase only)
Curve3  "Curve 3" 0 480 240 db -24 24 | Curve layer point 3 of 32 (log-spaced 20 Hz to 20 kHz, joined by a smooth curve), in dB, added to the bands before the linear-phase design (a match curve; Linear phase only)
